    <string name="voice_title">Voice calling</string>
    <string name="voice_explained">Names are matched on the phone first. When that isn\'t sure, an AI model on OpenRouter works out what she meant, using your API key. For that, what she said and contact names are sent to OpenRouter and the model\'s provider. Each request costs a tiny fraction of a cent. For family words like \"oğlum\", save the person under that name or add it to their other names. Without a key, the phone\'s own matching still works. Without internet, the phone may not understand her language, so she gets all her people to tap instead.</string>
    <string name="api_key">OpenRouter API key</string>
    <string name="voice_model">AI model (blank uses the tested default)</string>
    <string name="voice_hears_audio">Let the AI hear her voice directly</string>
    <string name="voice_hears_audio_explained">Instead of reading the phone\'s guess at her words, the model listens to a recording. OpenRouter needs at least $0.50 of balance for this. If it fails, the phone\'s recognizer takes over.</string>
